# This file is intentionally blank.
# It's used to ensure that the 'uploads' directory is tracked by Git,
# even if it's empty initially. User-uploaded files in this directory
# should ideally be added to .gitignore if they are not meant to be
# version controlled (e.g., in a production environment).
# For this project, we assume uploads might be part of the repo content
# or the user will manage .gitignore for uploads themselves.
